My second ascension, first for the tournament:

Given my lack of skill at Nethack, I was trying for the prize for
"Most unique deaths".  My first ten characters went just fine,
knocking off ten of the easier ways of dying.  Then #11, a Samurai,
was trying on random junk lying around the dungeon, hoping for a
spectacular death.  Unknown item #1: an amulet of change.  #2: A +1
ring of protection.  #3: +3 gauntlets of power.  Keep in mind that all
this was in the first two levels.  On level 3, I found another ring of
protection, this time at +2.  Given this luck, I figured I'd either
get an ascension, or a spectacular death.

I went down to the oracle level, and then decided to do the mines. 
The second level of the mines was a bonesfile from someone who'd died
by falling into a spiked pit.  I got a +1 mithril armor, +2 iron
shoes, a +1 elven helm, and a +1 cape of some sort out of that -- all
of them uncursed.  Minetown had no less than 3 magic markers and a
magic lamp that I used for light.  Sokoban had the amulet of
reflection, and another bones file (Hi, Austin!) gave me a bag of
holding (uncursed), Excalibur, and Mjollner.  After this, it was a
cakewalk.  A shop gave me a cloak of magic resistance.  I clobbered
Ashikaga Takauji in his sleep, with the help of an overzelous ninja. 
Medusa made the mistake of gazing into my amulet of reflection, and
the statue of Perseus gave me levitation boots.  I used the castle
wand (found at 0:3) for SDSM, a helm of brilliance, boots of speed, an
amulet of magic breathing, a spellbook of identify, and a ring of free
action.  I picked up three amulets of life saving in Gehennom, and
probably lost twice that many to monsters that were inconsiderate
enough to wear them -- not as if I ever needed life saving, but it was
reassuring to have along.

In Gehennom, I got all the demon princes hostile, thanks to Excalibur.
 Thanks to the +7 Excalibur, none of them was a problem.  Vlad went
down in short order, giving me the Candalabrum.  Rodney was
inconsiderate enough to drop the Book in the moat, but other than
that, he wasn't a problem.  After doing the invocation and getting the
"AoY, I only got one "mysterious force" pulling me down, and Rodney
didn't reappear until the Valley of the Dead.

Climbing up through the dungeon was easy -- I only had to whack Rodney
once -- and I made a brief stop at my stash for the artifacts I had
there.  Earth was easy, Air only a little harder (with one rest stop
inside a vortex to regain HP), Fire was fast -- I just ran past
everything, and Water was boring.

The Astral Plane was easy.  First altar, on the right, had Pesty and
was Chaotic.  #2, the middle, was Neutral, and had Famine.  Both of
those riders took two blows each to kill.  #3, with Death, was the
right one.  Death was something of a wimp, dying on the first blow.

Given this run of luck, I probably shouldn't try playing Nethack again
-- I'll never make it beyond the first level ;-)

P.S.  Have the priests, angels, and whatnot been toned down a bit in
the past few years, or was it just my incredible luck that kept me
from getting any summoning floods, and very few insects?

